      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) in the right prism \\(ABCDEF\\), we first need to identify the coordinates of points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\). The bases are equilateral triangles with side length 12, and the height of the prism is 16.\n\nLet's place the prism in a coordinate system for simplicity. Place vertex \\(A\\) at \\((0,0)\\), vertex \\(B\\) at \\((12,0)\\), and vertex \\(C\\) at \\((6,-6)\\) (since the length of each side of the equilateral triangle is 12). The vertex \\(D\\) will be directly above the midpoint of \\(BC\\) at \\((6,-6+8)= (6,-22)\\), \\(E\\) will be directly above \\(F\\) at \\((0,-16)\\), and \\(F\\) will be directly above \\(D\\) at \\((12,-16)\\).\n\nNow, we find the midpoints \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\):\n- Point \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\), so \\(X = \\left(\\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}\\right) = (3, -3)\\).\n- Point \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\), so \\(Y = \\left(\\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}\\right) = (9, -3)\\).\n- Point \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\), so \\(Z = \\left(\\frac{6+12}{2}, \\frac{-6-22}{2}\\right) = (9, -14)\\).\n\nNext, we calculate the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\):\n- The distance \\(XY\\) is:\n\\[\nXY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = 6\n\\]\n- The distance \\(YZ\\) is:\n\\[\nYZ = \\sqrt{(9-9)^2 + (-14+3)^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-11)^2} = 11\n\\]\n- The distance \\(XZ\\) is:\n\\[\nXZ = \\sqrt{(3-9)^2 + (-3+14)^2} = \\sqrt{(-6)^2 + 11^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 121} = \\sqrt{157}\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + XZ = 6 + 11 + \\sqrt{157} = 17 + \\sqrt{157}\n\\]\n\nHowever, upon re-evaluating the problem, we realize that the length of \\(XZ\\) should be calculated correctly as:\n\\[\nXZ = \\sqrt{(3-9)^2 + (-3-14)^2} = \\sqrt{(-6)^2 + (-17)^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 289} = \\sqrt{325} = 5\\sqrt{13}\n\\]\n\nThus, the correct perimeter is:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + XZ = 6 + 11 + 5\\sqrt{13} = 17 + 5\\sqrt{13}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{34}\n\\]",
