      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) in the given right prism \\(ABCDEF\\), we first need to find the lengths of the segments \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(ZX\\).\n\nThe base of the prism is an equilateral triangle with side length 12. Therefore, the coordinates of the vertices of the base triangle can be:\n- \\(A = (0, 0)\\),\n- \\(B = (12, 0)\\),\n- \\(C = (6, -6)\\).\n\nThe points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively. We can find the coordinates of these midpoints as follows:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\): \\(X = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3)\\).\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\): \\(Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3)\\).\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\): \\(Z = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-6-6}{2} \\right) = (6, -6)\\).\n\nNow, we need to calculate the lengths of \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(ZX\\):\n- The distance \\(XY\\) is calculated using the distance formula:\n  \\[\n  XY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6.\n  \\]\n- The distance \\(YZ\\) is calculated as follows:\n  \\[\n  YZ = \\sqrt{(6-9)^2 + (-6+3)^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + (-3)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 9} = \\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2}.\n  \\]\n- The distance \\(ZX\\) is calculated as follows:\n  \\[\n  ZX = \\sqrt{(6-3)^2 + (-6+3)^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-3)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 9} = \\sqrt{18} = 3\\sqrt{2}.\n  \\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\nXY + YZ + ZX = 6 + 3\\sqrt{2} + 3\\sqrt{2} = 6 + 6\\sqrt{2}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{6 + 6\\sqrt{2}}\\).",
